<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia Yield Spreads-Outpaced by Canada.</title>
<headline>Australia Yield Spreads-Outpaced by Canada.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> AUD VS   3-YR	   10-YR	* AUD 3-YR/10-YR SPREAD</p>
<p> USD	-42 (+ 08)    53 (- 03) * FUTURES   122   (- 05)</p>
<p> CAD	 93 (+ 18)    80 (+ 04) * CASH	123   (- 06)</p>
<p> NZD     -100 (+ 03)   -13 (- 03) *</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Australian debt market was fairly mixed against the dollar bloc after Thursday's sharp tightening, although it was clearly outpaced by Canada.  </p>
<p>Although the local market remains on hold for a further easing in monetary policy, Canada took to heart Thursday's U.S. retail sales data, which showed a third successive fall, as a further sign that the Federal Reserve will not tighten in July.</p>
<p>Canadian debt rallied strongly on Thursday and the 30-year spread to the U.S. went to a negative for the first time.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
